Maya Patel: quick heads-up  our new next-starter-agent sample failed the eval parity run. Looks like SDK retry + agent step ordering cause double-execution on a 401 retry.

Maya Patel: Repro: clone examples/next-starter-agent, yarn dev, set REDWOOD_TEST_EXPIRE_MS=700, call /api/run-agent. Sometimes the agent logs two identical tool calls after a 401.

Liam O'Connor: saw that locally. Log: 'ToolInvoke: embeddings.create called twice for same input' after auth refresh retried the second step.

Zoe Kim: snippet from pages/api/agent.js:```js
const agent = new Agent({ tools });
const resp = await agent.run({ query });
res.json(resp);
```

Samir Gupta: likely cause: agent runtime retries an internal tool call when SDK does a transparent retry; the agent also has its own step retry on transient failures, so they combine into double-invoke. We should ensure SDK retries are only for idempotent endpoints and agent runtime marks tool calls with idempotent flag when safe.

Maya Patel: temporary unblock for eval: set REDWOOD_SDK_ASSUME_RETRY=true and in the agent tool wrappers set opts.idempotent = true for embeddings and read-only tools. That unblocks parity while we fix.

Liam O'Connor: proposed SDK change: when doing automated 401 refresh retry, only retry if opts.idempotent === true or method in SAFE_METHODS. Also export a helper markIdempotent(tool) for agent authors.

Zoe Kim: agent change (pseudo):```js
function wrapTool(tool) {
  return async (input) => {
    return sdk.call('embeddings.create', { input, idempotent: true });
  }
}
```

Samir Gupta: added a tiny test in examples that forces expiry and asserts single tool invocation. Will open PR with test + example agent change.

devex-bot: CI job: https://ci.internal.redwood/gh/examples/next-starter-agent/14 -> tests/eval/parity -> 2476543228

Maya Patel: small doc note: agents that call external write ops (datastores, task queues) should never mark them idempotent. We need agent template README to call this out.

Liam O'Connor: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/examples/pull/207 includes test fixture + README note. SDK PR WIP to gate retries on idempotent flag.

Zoe Kim: once SDK patch lands we can remove CI env toggle and re-run strict parity. Thanks all for quick triage.
